f-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Kent County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years. In 2026 so far, the middle of the grids sat at 49% of normal for February to March and 52% for March to April. Every grid had its driest year in 1965, and grid 23319 got 54% of normal that year.</p>"}
